[h1]Flavorium Universalis v0.4.1: Ministers and Offices[/h1]

[i]Compatible with EU5 1.4.* | Multiplayer synchronized[/i]

[hr][/hr]

[h2]Cabinet efficiency[/h2]

The 0.4.0 increase made cabinet efficiency too strong, because most of it applied to every minister at once. More of it now belongs to the minister who earns it.

[list]
[*] [b]Traits:[/b] cabinet efficiency from cabinet traits (eight traits, including the efficiency administrator and the age traits) now improves only the minister who has the trait, not the whole cabinet. The negative trait works the same way.
[*] [b]Experience:[/b] the service record a minister builds with experience now gives +4% cabinet efficiency and +3% cabinet trait impact per level above the first, to that minister only. At level 10 that is +36% and +27%.
[*] Household offices still grant cabinet efficiency to the whole cabinet.
[/list]

[h2]Household offices[/h2]

[list]
[*] [b]Automation:[/b] each card on the Household tab has an automation toggle (the gear). An automated post that stands open is filled at the start of each month by the most senior minister trained for it and free of other posts, at the usual appointment cost. Up to 6 posts can be automated, the same as the household's cap. A sitting holder is never replaced, and dismissing a holder turns automation off for that post.
[*] [b]Costs on the cards:[/b] every card has a Costs line again: the household upkeep each filled post adds, plus any cost of the post itself. A post's own cost does not grow with the holder's seniority.
[*] [b]Court spending efficiency[/b] is now granted only by the Court Chamberlain (+8%, was +12%) and the Keeper of the Wardrobe (+7%, was +10%). The other offices that gave it now do something of their own:
[list]
[*] Master of the Mint: -0.05% monthly inflation and +5% minting income.
[*] Master of Coin: +3% tax income efficiency.
[*] Seneschal: +1% monthly control.
[*] Consistory Superintendent: +0.05 monthly religious influence.
[*] Master of Siege Works: +5% fort maintenance efficiency.
[/list]
[*] [b]Posts with a cost:[/b] Grand Inquisitor (-1 tolerance of heretics), Constable and Keeper of the Kurultai (-2% crown power each), Hansa Factor (-5% burghers satisfaction), State Inquisitor (-0.5 diplomatic reputation), Court Astrologer (-0.02 monthly prestige).
[*] [b]New secondary effects:[/b] Keeper of the Wardrobe -10% artist salaries, Keeper of the Chronicles +5% skill of new artists, State Inquisitor +10% spy network construction, Master of the Road +10% tariff income, Postelnic +5 subject loyalty.
[/list]

[h2]Schools[/h2]

[list]
[*] [b]The rival university is on your continent.[/b] The rival that courts your masters and draws your students was the most prominent university anywhere in the world, so a school in Constantinople could lose its headmaster to one in Vietnam. It is now the leading foreign university on your capital's continent. A school's rank on its card is still among all the world's universities.
[*] [b]A dormant school could not be refilled.[/b] Enrol in School needed a living school member somewhere in the realm, so a school with none could never take a student. It now needs a founded school, and enrolling someone wakes it.
[/list]

[h2]Localization[/h2]

French, German and Spanish are updated for the changed offices and schools.
